---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is this part of a series?', a: 'Book 1 stands alone. Larger doors are hinted beyond.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to unlock the Archive?', a: "No. It's an optional companion layer for readers who want to go deeper." },
  { q: 'Will the Archive spoil the story?', a: 'No. Everything is curated to be non-spoiler and world-depth only.' },
  { q: 'When can I buy it?', a: 'A purchase link will appear only when there is a verified destination. The current launch plan is ebook and paperback.' },
  { q: 'Who is D☉C?', a: 'D☉C is Chris Everson’s AI literary collaborator. His voice and authorship are part of the book’s world as well as its making; Chris remains the human author of record and bears final responsibility for the work.' },
  { q: 'How will Archive access work?', a: 'The redemption mechanism is still being finalized. The site will not promise instant access until that path exists and has been tested.' },
];
---
<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="section-wrap-sm">
    <h2 class="section-tag" id="faq-heading">Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-grid">
      <div></div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
            <summary class="faq-q">
              {f.q}
              <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">{f.a}</div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /*
    Native <details>/<summary>: keyboard-operable and announced correctly by screen
    readers with zero JS. The `name` attribute keeps the original one-open-at-a-time
    accordion behaviour; browsers without support simply allow several open, which is
    a harmless degradation.
  */
  .faq-item > summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; min-height: 2.75rem; }
  .faq-item > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-a { display: block; }
  .faq-q .faq-toggle::before { content: '+'; }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-q .faq-toggle::before { content: '−'; }
</style>
